{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bgv48k9w7","tool_use_id":"toolu_01CGHWaPbgZkKp8Yy2gtttEA","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run3-repo/3da34d2a-47ac-4f88-8b30-06488b931e98/tasks/bgv48k9w7.output","summary":"Background command \"cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop; D=iter_2/candidate_2\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nPeople judge a sequence random to the extent their own model of a fair coin (with a person-specific belief about how often it switches) explains it better than the regular generators they suspect (a switch-biased Markov coin, a trick coin, and a repeating short motif with slips, with each person's own readiness to suspect a motif), weighing the evidence per flip by a fitted power of length. The single claim is that the trick coin people imagine is not symmetric: they suspect a coin rigged towards heads (the side a cheat would favour) more than one rigged towards tails, so a surplus of heads is taken as evidence of rigging while an equal surplus of tails is not. The model disagrees most sharply with the current best (H/T-symmetric) model on pairs of mirror-image or count-mismatched sequences, e.g. HHTHHH versus TTHTTT, where it predicts the tail-heavy sequence is chosen as more random — addressing the FDR-surviving critique that people choose the sequence with more heads less often than a symmetric model allows.\nEOF\necho heads_rigged_trick_coin_suspicion > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'PY'\nsrc=open(\"models/person_specific_motif_suspicion.py\").read()\ndoc_old=src.split('\"\"\"')[1]\nsrc=src.replace(doc_old,\"\"\"Heads-rigged trick-coin suspicion in the Bayesian chance-vs-regular judgment.\n\nPeople judge a sequence random to the extent their own fair coin (person-specific\nbelieved switch rate) explains it better than the regular generators (Markov coin,\ntrick coin, repeating motif with slips and person-specific motif suspicion),\nweighed per flip by (n / 5) ** -gamma, with person-specific sensitivity.\n\nSingle claim: the trick coin people imagine is asymmetric — its heads rate has a\nBeta(2*sigmoid(s), 2*(1 - sigmoid(s))) prior with fitted asymmetry s, so with s > 0\na surplus of heads is evidence of rigging and an equal surplus of tails is not;\nthe model is no longer H/T symmetric, and predicts tail-heavy sequences are chosen\nas more random than their head-heavy mirror images.\n\"\"\",1)\nsrc=src.replace('''    out = {\"k\": float(k), \"lm\": log_markov, \"lb\": log_biased}''','''    out = {\"k\": float(k), \"lm\": log_markov, \"lb\": log_biased, \"h\": float(h)}''')\nsrc=src.replace('''        \"seq_len\": np.asarray([t[\"n\"] for t in table], dtype=\"float64\"),\n    }''','''        \"seq_len\": np.asarray([t[\"n\"] for t in table], dtype=\"float64\"),\n        \"seq_heads\": np.asarray([t[\"h\"] for t in table], dtype=\"float64\"),\n    }''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    seq_len = pm.Data(\"seq_len\", np.full(1, 2.0))\n''','''    seq_len = pm.Data(\"seq_len\", np.full(1, 2.0))\n    seq_heads = pm.Data(\"seq_heads\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    # Log marginal likelihood of each distinct''','''    # Asymmetric trick coin: heads-rate prior Beta(a_h, a_t), a_h + a_t = 2\n    # (s = 0 recovers the uniform, symmetric prior).\n    s_asym = pm.Normal(\"s_asym\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n    a_h = 2.0 * pm.math.sigmoid(s_asym)\n    a_t = 2.0 - a_h\n    seq_lbias_asym = (\n        pt.gammaln(seq_heads + a_h)\n        + pt.gammaln(seq_len - seq_heads + a_t)\n        - pt.gammaln(seq_len + 2.0)\n        - pt.gammaln(a_h)\n        - pt.gammaln(a_t)\n    )\n\n    # Log marginal likelihood of each distinct''')\nsrc=src.replace(\"seq_lbias[idx]\",\"seq_lbias_asym[idx]\")\nopen(\"iter_2/candidate_2/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nPY\ngrep -n \"seq_lbias\" $D/candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_2 --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"7a03427e-af3f-4091-9932-98352183699d","session_id":"3da34d2a-47ac-4f88-8b30-06488b931e98"}
